==History==
2016
*The Mirror [[Cards|card]] was added with Clash Royale's game launch on 4/1/2016.
*On 2/2/2016, the [[Version History#February 2016 Update (2/2/2016)|February 2016 Update]], increased the Mirrored {{Rarity|Common}} cards Level by 4 and Mirrored {{Rarity|Rare}} cards Level by 2.
*On 29/2/2016, the [[Version History#March%202016%20Update%20(29/2/2016)|March 2016 Update]], changed the Mirror's card image. It was also fixed a bug that caused the player to receive 1 [[Elixir]] after using Mirror, effectively refunding the +1 Elixir cost.
*On 23/3/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (23/3/2016)|Balance Update]], decreased the Mirrored {{Rarity|Legendary}} cards Level by 1.
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May 2016 Update (3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], increased the Mirrored {{Rarity|Common}} and {{Rarity|Rare}} cards Level by 1. It also changed the Mirror by making it count as a 1.5 [[Elixir]] card when calculating the Average Elixir Cost of a [[Battle Decks|deck]]. Before the update, it was simply ignored in calculating the average cost as if the deck had only 7 cards.
*On 19/9/2016, the [[Version History#September 2016 Update (19/9/2016)|September 2016 Update]], increased all Mirrored cards Level by 1. This allows players with Level 8 Mirror to deploy Level 14 cards, which would be unobtainable otherwise.
*On 2/11/2016, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (2/11/2016)|maintenance break]], decreased the Level 8 Mirror's Mirrored card Level by 1. This was to fix a bug where cards above the max Level did not appear.
*On 15/12/2016, the [[Version History#December 2016 Update (15/12/2016)|December 2016 Update]], increased the Level 8 Mirror's Mirrored card Level by 1; the bug above was finally fixed.
2018
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], changed the Mirror such that, if used in a deck, will never appear as one of the cards in the player's opening hand. It also moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Mirror from Spell Valley to Electro Valley.
*On 27/6/2018, an [[Version History#Optional Update (27/6/2018)|Optional Update]], changed the Mirror such that it will never appear as one of the cards in the player's opening hand during [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Draft]] battles.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8).
*On 5/12/2018, the [[Version History#December%202018%20Update%20(5/12/2018)|December 2018 Update]], changed the Mirror's card description, adding the phrase "''Will not appear in your starting cards''" to it.
2019
*On 28/1/2019, the [[Version History#January%202019%20Update%20(28/1/2019)|January 2019 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Mirror from Electro Valley to Spooky Town.
*On 13/2/2019, an [[Version History#Optional Update (13/2/2019)|Optional Update]], made it so that mirroring [[Three Musketeers]] would no longer display the cost of 11 Elixir.
*On 15/4/2019, the [[Version History#April%202019%20Update%20(15/4/2019)|April 2019 Update]], changed the Mirror's card description. Previously, its description was "''Mirrors your last card played for +1 Elixir. Will not appear in your starting cards.''"
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]], removed the Mirror from all Draft selections.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], gave the Mirror a new animation if a card has been mirrored. A Mirror appears on the ground with the new card, in addition to a special sound effect.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], fixed the missing Mirror deployment animation.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13). It also added a card render to the Mirror's card info screen.
2022
*On 4/4/2022, the [[Version History#April%202022%20Update%20(4/4/2022)|April 2022 Update]], increased all Mirrored cards Level by 1. This allows players with Level 14 Mirror to deploy Level 16 cards, which would be unobtainable otherwise.
*On 12/9/2022, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (12/9/2022)|maintenance break]], reverted the Mirror to its state before 4/4/2022. More specifically, it decreased all Mirrored cards Level by 1, making a Level 14 Mirror deploy Level 15 cards once again.
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], made it so that the Mirror is unusable immediately after using a {{Rarity|Champion}} card. It also moved the Arena to unlock the Mirror from Spooky Town to Miner's Mine.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 16/12/2024, the [[Version History#2024 Quarter 4 Update (16/12/2024)|2024 Quarter 4 Update]], fixed a bug where Mirror would show a question mark instead of its Elixir cost.
2025
*On 29/9/2025, the [[Version_History/2025#2025 Quarter 3 Update (29/9/2025)|2025 Quarter 3 Update]], made the Mirror able to copy a {{Rarity|Champion}} card.

