==Trivia==
*The word "''Mirror''" comes from the Latin "''mīrus''", meaning wonderful. The earliest manufactured mirrors were pieces of polished stone such as obsidian, a naturally occurring volcanic glass. Examples of obsidian mirrors found at Çatalhöyük in Anatolia have been dated to around 6000 BCE. Mirrors are still used to this day for multiple applications, whether that is for transportation, architecture, or general aesthetics.
*The Mirror is the only [[Cards|card]] in the game that does not have a defined [[Elixir]] cost. However, the cost will always be at least 2 and at most 10, as there are no other cards that cost less than 1 or more than 9.
**When calculating the Average Elixir Cost of a [[Battle Decks|deck]], the Mirror is treated as a 1.5 Elixir card. Before the [[Version History#May 2016 Update (3/5/16)|May 2016 Update]], it was simply ignored in calculating the average cost as if the deck had only 7 cards.
**Mirror is grouped with [[:Category:1-Elixir Cards|1 Elixir cards]] when sorting them by Elixir in-game.
**While there are no [[:Category:10-Elixir Cards|10 Elixir cards]] currently, a 10 Elixir card would still cost 10 Elixir after mirroring it.
*The Mirror is 1 of 2 cards which does not appear in the player's starting hand, with the other being [[Elixir Collector]].
*The upgrades work like that of a [[Clone]]. When leveling up the Mirror, the mirrored cards' Level will be increased.
*The Mirror is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 2 cards that is unavailable in Draft, the other being Clone.
**It is 1 of 9 cards that is unavailable in Triple Draft, the others being [[Three Musketeers]], [[Giant Skeleton]] and Clone
**It is 1 of 2 cards that is unavailable in Mega Draft, the others being Clone.
**It is 1 of 3 cards that cannot be set on Defense Towers in [[Clan Wars]], the others being Elixir Collector and Clone.
*While upgrading it, the card will show its original card image. This is likely a bug ot oversight.

